// Hunt: Heavy string concatenation obfuscation in script content
// Table: DeviceCustomScriptEvents
// Purpose: Obfuscation tools such as Invoke-Obfuscation commonly split a
//          sensitive keyword like Invoke-Expression into many short quoted
//          fragments joined with the + operator, to defeat simple keyword
//          matching. A high raw count of + operators on a single script
//          content value is a cheap, robust heuristic for this pattern and
//          avoids fragile quote escaped regex.
// Validated: success, rows returned against live SOC-Central data (7 day window).
//          Threshold of 8 is tuned from real samples; raise it if a specific
//          environment has legitimately math heavy scripts and generates
//          excess noise.
DeviceCustomScriptEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(7d)
| where isnotempty(ScriptContent)
| extend ConcatHits = countof(ScriptContent, '+')
| where ConcatHits >= 8
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, InitiatingProcessFileName, ConcatHits, RuleName
| order by ConcatHits desc
| take 10000
